Add attendee self-registration, for logged-in users with any authentication plugin and, when allowed, anonymous visitors who confirm their email address. Each event opts in with an Attendees database, which has a registration prefix, a confirmation policy, a registration deadline that ends registration even while the database is open, and a created, open and closed workflow. The database is a page with blocks that starts with the registration block, so it is the registration page of the event; while open, it is public and shows in the navigation, but only organizers can list its registrations. Registrations are named with codes such as `PYC26-7KQ3M9XD`, move through the pending, registered, attended and cancelled states, and are handled by the new `@registration` endpoint on the event root and `@attendees` endpoint on the Attendees database. @ericof
